From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 20:20:14 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] soc: apple: mailbox: Hold the receive side across system
 sleep on request

The receive IRQ of the ASC mailboxes is IRQF_NO_SUSPEND, so every
coprocessor message wakes a CPU out of suspend-to-idle. On the J713
the GPU firmware's idle ring-service kicks and an AOP report every
second wake it about three times a second: in 938 s of s2idle, 1472
wakeups and only 512 s in deep idle.

For a mailbox marked apple,hold-rx-in-sleep, mask the receive IRQ from
noirq suspend to noirq resume, so its messages wait in the FIFO and the
consumer handles them on resume. The mailbox is a supplier of its
consumer, so this runs after the consumer suspended and before it
resumes. The firmware throttles once its outbox fills: after 148 s of
s2idle, 11 GPU and 3 AOP messages were waiting, with 3 wakeups and
146.9 s in deep idle.

Signed-off-by: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>
(cherry picked from commit 7c5a1efc5f04b4904f94aafa7b9ade890c1e4dd1)
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
---
 drivers/soc/apple/mailbox.c       | 30 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 include/linux/soc/apple/mailbox.h |  2 ++
 2 files changed, 32 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/apple/mailbox.c b/drivers/soc/apple/mailbox.c
index 5be648a40f..7ffe2b1367 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/apple/mailbox.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/apple/mailbox.c
@@ -643,6 +643,7 @@ static int apple_mbox_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 		return -ENOMEM;
 
 	mbox->dev = &pdev->dev;
+	mbox->hold_rx_in_sleep = of_property_read_bool(dev->of_node, "apple,hold-rx-in-sleep");
 	mbox->hw = of_device_get_match_data(dev);
 	if (!mbox->hw)
 		return -EINVAL;
@@ -897,10 +898,39 @@ static const struct of_device_id apple_mbox_of_match[] = {
 };
 MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(of, apple_mbox_of_match);
 
+/*
+ * The receive IRQ is IRQF_NO_SUSPEND, so each message wakes a CPU out of
+ * suspend-to-idle. A coprocessor whose messages need not wake the system
+ * keeps them in the FIFO until resume. The mailbox is a supplier of its
+ * consumer, so this runs after the consumer suspended and before it resumes.
+ */
+static int apple_mbox_suspend_noirq(struct device *dev)
+{
+	struct apple_mbox *mbox = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
+
+	if (mbox && mbox->hold_rx_in_sleep)
+		apple_mbox_hold_rx(mbox);
+	return 0;
+}
+
+static int apple_mbox_resume_noirq(struct device *dev)
+{
+	struct apple_mbox *mbox = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
+
+	if (mbox && mbox->hold_rx_in_sleep)
+		apple_mbox_release_rx(mbox);
+	return 0;
+}
+
+static const struct dev_pm_ops apple_mbox_pm_ops = {
+	NOIRQ_SYSTEM_SLEEP_PM_OPS(apple_mbox_suspend_noirq, apple_mbox_resume_noirq)
+};
+
 static struct platform_driver apple_mbox_driver = {
 	.driver = {
 		.name = "apple-mailbox",
 		.of_match_table = apple_mbox_of_match,
+		.pm = pm_sleep_ptr(&apple_mbox_pm_ops),
 	},
 	.probe = apple_mbox_probe,
 	.remove = apple_mbox_remove,
diff --git a/include/linux/soc/apple/mailbox.h b/include/linux/soc/apple/mailbox.h
index fcb17eaf2d..6cbf100d03 100644
--- a/include/linux/soc/apple/mailbox.h
+++ b/include/linux/soc/apple/mailbox.h
@@ -64,6 +64,8 @@ struct apple_mbox {
 	bool active;
 	bool ascwrap_v6_cpu_running;
 	bool removing;
+	/* apple,hold-rx-in-sleep: receive IRQ masked across system sleep */
+	bool hold_rx_in_sleep;
 
 	int irq_recv_not_empty;
 	int irq_send_empty; /* < 0: no send-empty IRQ, TX polls */
